<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Surena</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 52 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Surena was a Parthian general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-suren">House of Suren</a> in the service of King Orodes II. In 53 BCE at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-carrhae">Carrhae</a>, using <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horse-archer">horse archers</a> kept supplied with arrows by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camel">camel</a> train and heavy cataphract cavalry, he destroyed a much larger Roman army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-licinius-crassus">Marcus Licinius Crassus</a>, who was killed. Soon afterwards Orodes, apparently fearing his power, had him put to death.</p></div>
